## Behavioral Language Primitives

The following is a list of primitve transformations that the engine can compute. Some of the entries have already been implemented, while others are simply a definition that will be implemented.

These primitives are a declarative semantic rule that the engine can execute to derive the expected post-state, not an implementation of how the program performs the operation.

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> The list below is ongoing and will be populated as the Behavioral Language is defined further.

### Axiomatic Primitives
- [Get Primitive](/src/ExecutableModelTest/SemanticPrimitives/GetPrimitive/readme)
- [Set Primitive](/src/ExecutableModelTest/SemanticPrimitives/SetPrimitive/readme)
- [Create Primitive](/src/ExecutableModelTest/SemanticPrimitives/CreatePrimitive/readme)
- [Remove Primitive](/src/ExecutableModelTest/SemanticPrimitives/RemovePrimitive/readme)
- [Insert Primitive](/src/ExecutableModelTest/SemanticPrimitives/InsertPrimitive/readme)
- [GetFromPos Primitive](/src/ExecutableModelTest/SemanticPrimitives/GetFromPosPrimitive/readme)

### Derived Primitives
- Transfer Primitive

